{
  "_comment": [
    "Declarative registry for scripts/normalise.py. No parsing logic lives here.",
    "models are tried in order: the first pattern that matches wins, so more",
    "specific models (iPad Air, Magic Keyboard for iPad Air) precede generic",
    "ones (iPad). 'emit' lists the configuration axes that participate in the",
    "product_id; the code always writes them in the canonical SLUG_AXIS_ORDER.",
    "'required' lists the axes that must be present after defaults are applied;",
    "it defaults to 'emit' when omitted.",
    "'defaults' are catalogue-anchored axes the Apple JSON-LD page title omits",
    "for the current generation. They never override a value found in the",
    "title, and a default that would alias a different catalogue configuration",
    "raises NormalisationCollision instead of merging."
  ],
